--- Finding (metaprogramming): a function called with a list of ints, a list of
--- floats and a list of any third kind (text, bools, lists) is an internal error
--- in both modes, before the program runs. It is the spec's own Specialization
--- example (`first` of `[1, 2, 3]` and of `['a', 'b']`) with a list of floats
--- added.
---
--- crow run -i and crow run alike (exit 1, nothing printed):
---   metaprogramming-2.co: internal error: the lowered program disagrees with
---   itself — a bug in Crow, not in this program: metaprogramming-2 main: line 25:
---   hands 'first__1' Tensor(Float, [1]) for its parameter 'xs' (argument 1),
---   which is Tensor(Int, [2])
--- Expected:
---   1
---   2.5
---   a
--- Any two of the three calls run in both modes and print their answers, in
--- either order; the three fail in any order. Found showing a function written
--- once and compiled per kind (`largest` of ints, floats and text). Perhaps the
--- root of findings/k_d_tree-2.co (matrices of ints and of floats beside a third
--- signature).
fn first[xs]
    return xs[0]

log[first[[1, 2]]]
log[first[[2.5]]]
log[first[['a']]]
